{"content":[{"c":["GOD-FEARER"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One who fears God. This can be a term of reverence, an emotional reaction of terror, or a dread of God’s vengeance."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Phrases describing the God-fearer in the OT are frequently coupled with such terms as “stood in awe” and “held in awe” (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.16.25","r":"1Chr.16.25","rawR":"1Chr.16.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.16.25","value":"1Chr.16.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 16:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.22.23","r":"Ps.22.23","rawR":"Ps.22.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.22.23","value":"Ps.22.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 22:23"},"). Reverence for the Lord is used less frequently, but it is used with this meaning when Obadiah hid the prophets in a cave to save them from being assassinated by Jezebel (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.18.3-4,12","r":"1Kgs.18.3-4,12","rawR":"1Kgs.18.3-4,12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.18.3-4,12","value":"1Kgs.18.3-4,12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 18:3-4, 12"},"). A man could expect to receive justice from a God-fearing ruler (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.3","r":"2Sam.23.3","rawR":"2Sam.23.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.3","value":"2Sam.23.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.19.7","r":"2Chr.19.7","rawR":"2Chr.19.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.19.7","value":"2Chr.19.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 19:7"},"), and long life was a reward for those who feared the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.10.27","r":"Pr.10.27","rawR":"Pr.10.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.10.27","value":"Pr.10.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 10:27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Pr.14.27","r":"Pr.14.27","rawR":"Pr.14.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.14.27","value":"Pr.14.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Pr.19.23","r":"Pr.19.23","rawR":"Pr.19.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.19.23","value":"Pr.19.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:23"},"). A God-fearing family would rely on the Lord for practical help in time of trouble (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.4.1","r":"2Kgs.4.1","rawR":"2Kgs.4.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.4.1","value":"2Kgs.4.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 4:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Pr.14.26","r":"Pr.14.26","rawR":"Pr.14.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.14.26","value":"Pr.14.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 14:26"},"). The fear of the Lord was effective in driving away sin and was itself the beginning of wisdom (",{"href":"?bref=Wisd.10.13","r":"Wisd.10.13","rawR":"Wisd.10.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Wisd.10.13","value":"Wisd.10.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Wisd of Sol 10:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["In the NT fear of God is frequently used in conjunction with admonitions to love and serve the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Col.3.22","r":"Col.3.22","rawR":"Col.3.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Col.3.22","value":"Col.3.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Col 3:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Pet.2.17","r":"1Pet.2.17","rawR":"1Pet.2.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Pet.2.17","value":"1Pet.2.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Pt 2:17"},"). In the Magnificat, Mary’s statement “His mercy is on those who fear him” is used in the sense of revere and obey (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.1.50","r":"Luke.1.50","rawR":"Luke.1.50","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.1.50","value":"Luke.1.50"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 1:50"},"). In Acts, the term “God-fearer” is given a specific interpretation, being used with reference to Gentiles who attended the synagogue. Paul mentions them separately when introducing his address: “Men of Israel, and you that fear God” (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.13.16","r":"Acts.13.16","rawR":"Acts.13.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.13.16","value":"Acts.13.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 13:16"},", ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). Cornelius was an honest, generous, and God-fearing Roman centurion who, although not a Jew, was recognized as leading a life acceptable to the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.10.2,35","r":"Acts.10.2,35","rawR":"Acts.10.2,35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.10.2,35","value":"Acts.10.2,35"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:2, 35"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["The fear of God was also used in both the OT and the NT to denote dread or terror of the mighty power and judgment of the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.3.10","r":"Gen.3.10","rawR":"Gen.3.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.3.10","value":"Gen.3.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 3:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.9.19","r":"Deut.9.19","rawR":"Deut.9.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.9.19","value":"Deut.9.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 9:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.6.4","r":"Job.6.4","rawR":"Job.6.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.6.4","value":"Job.6.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jb 6:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Job.9.28-29","r":"Job.9.28-29","rawR":"Job.9.28-29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.9.28-29","value":"Job.9.28-29"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:28-29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.76.8","r":"Ps.76.8","rawR":"Ps.76.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.76.8","value":"Ps.76.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 76:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.17.7","r":"Matt.17.7","rawR":"Matt.17.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.17.7","value":"Matt.17.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 17:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.28.10","r":"Matt.28.10","rawR":"Matt.28.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.28.10","value":"Matt.28.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"28:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.5.10","r":"Luke.5.10","rawR":"Luke.5.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.5.10","value":"Luke.5.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 5:10"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.12.5","r":"Luke.12.5","rawR":"Luke.12.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.12.5","value":"Luke.12.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Acts.5.5,11","r":"Acts.5.5,11","rawR":"Acts.5.5,11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.5.5,11","value":"Acts.5.5,11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 5:5, 11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Tim.5.20","r":"1Tim.5.20","rawR":"1Tim.5.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Tim.5.20","value":"1Tim.5.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Tm 5:20"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Fear_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Fear_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Fear_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Fear"},"; ",{"href":"?item=Proselyte_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Proselyte_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Proselyte_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Proselyte"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"GodFearer","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 16:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.16.25","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.16.25","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.16.25"},{"anchorText":"Ps 22:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.22.23","rawQueryValue":"Ps.22.23","sourceRefExact":"Ps.22.23"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 18:3-4, 12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.18.3-4,12","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.18.3-4,12","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.18.3-4,12"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.3","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.3","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.3"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 19:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.19.7","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.19.7","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.19.7"},{"anchorText":"Prv 10:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.10.27","rawQueryValue":"Pr.10.27","sourceRefExact":"Pr.10.27"},{"anchorText":"14:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.14.27","rawQueryValue":"Pr.14.27","sourceRefExact":"Pr.14.27"},{"anchorText":"19:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.19.23","rawQueryValue":"Pr.19.23","sourceRefExact":"Pr.19.23"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 4:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.4.1","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.4.1","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.4.1"},{"anchorText":"Prv 14:26","canonicalization":"